From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: do not re-claim host in the IRQ callback

The MMC SDIO core invokes a function IRQ callback while the host is already
claimed by the SDIO IRQ worker.  The callback contract explicitly requires the
handler not to call sdio_claim_host() or sdio_release_host().

The P4 port uses bytewise CMD52 access for the ESP slave register window.
esp_handle_isr() therefore performs several synchronous commands while holding
that already-claimed host.  Passing ACQUIRE_LOCK makes esp_read_reg() and
esp_write_reg() perform a nested claim/release around the callback's
transaction.  Avoid that unnecessary ownership transition in the callback and
leave all non-IRQ callers unchanged.

This is a P4 host-side synchronization fix.  It does not change the C6 image,
register addresses, command format, retry policy, or DMA path.

---
 sdio/esp_sdio.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sdio/esp_sdio.c b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -399,1 +399,1 @@
-			(u8 *) int_status, sizeof(*int_status), ACQUIRE_LOCK);
+			(u8 *) int_status, sizeof(*int_status), LOCK_ALREADY_ACQUIRED);
@@ -408,1 +408,1 @@
-				(u8 *) &raw, sizeof(raw), ACQUIRE_LOCK);
+				(u8 *) &raw, sizeof(raw), LOCK_ALREADY_ACQUIRED);
@@ -429,1 +429,1 @@
-					ACQUIRE_LOCK);
+					LOCK_ALREADY_ACQUIRED);
@@ -493,1 +493,1 @@
-			(u8 *) int_status, sizeof(*int_status), ACQUIRE_LOCK);
+			(u8 *) int_status, sizeof(*int_status), LOCK_ALREADY_ACQUIRED);
